41-compile-text: curry.compile of Curry text in both modes.

Seam: a module from text with a generated name and with modulename, a
reused name, imports by a module object and by a library name, mode='expr'
with imports and exprtype, a str given to eval, overloaded text without a
type, a syntax error.  The text of Nat.curry is compiled as text; the
oracle loads the same file as a module.
Sources: memo A7, A15; catalogue P12, P26, P32, P45; examples 02 and 18.
Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle: oracle.out (PAKCS 3.4.1 on the goals that are
plain Curry).

Expected output: the anonymous module is sprite__interactive_0; the second
compile under 'Named' is a ValueError; imports=[Nat] works and
imports=['Data.List'] is a KeyError (P32) where the import line of the
text works; natFromInt 3 is I (I (I O)); eval('natToInt O') is the string
itself (P12); 'toEnum 65' is a CompileError without a type and 'A' with
exprtype='Char'; a syntax error is a CompileError, printed by its class
because its text holds a path (P45).  Pins no defect.
